{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.singlet_forces_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.singlet_forces_three","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L176-L187","doc":"**The singlet pins the flavour dimension.**  A one-dimensional alternating\nchannel forces exactly three flavours: `C(N,3) = 1 ↔ N = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.decuplet_forces_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.decuplet_forces_three","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L159-L174","doc":"**The decuplet determines the flavour dimension.**  If the symmetric\nchannel has dimension 10 then `N = 3` — so the decuplet is not merely\n*consistent with* three flavours, it *forces* them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.eightfold_channels_at_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.eightfold_channels_at_three","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L152-L157","doc":"At `N = 3`: symmetric `10` (decuplet), mixed `8` (octet, with multiplicity\n`2`), alternating `1` (singlet); total `27 = 3³` — the eightfold way. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:borromean-decuplet","label":"prop:borromean-decuplet","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/borromean-decuplet-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.eightfold_channels_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.eightfold_channels_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L142-L150","doc":"At `N = 2`: symmetric `4`, mixed contributes `4`, alternating **`0`**;\ntotal `8 = 2³`.\n\nThe symmetric channel is a 4-dimensional spin-`3/2` quadruplet, not a decuplet,\nand there is no singlet at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.schur_weyl_cube_split_two_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.schur_weyl_cube_split_two_three","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L120-L138","doc":"**Dimension count at the two decisive values.**  The Specht\nmultiplicities `1, 2, 1` times the Weyl dimensions account for all of\n`V^{⊗3}` at `N = 2` and at `N = 3`:\n\n    N = 2 :   4 + 2·2 + 0  =  8  = 2³\n    N = 3 :  10 + 2·8 + 1  = 27  = 3³\n\nso nothing is missing from the three channels, and the `N = 2` deficit is\nlocated precisely in the vanishing alternating channel rather than in some\nunaccounted-for piece.\n\nThe general identity `N³ = C(N+2,3) + 4·C(N+1,3) + C(N,3)` for all `N` is\nWorpitzky's identity with Eulerian numbers `⟨3,k⟩ = 1, 4, 1`; it is **not**\nformalised here (it is standard, and the chapter compares only `N = 2` against\n`N = 3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.singlet_nonempty_forces_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.singlet_nonempty_forces_three","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L109-L112","doc":"A nonempty singlet channel forces at least three flavours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.no_singlet_of_lt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.no_singlet_of_lt_three","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L105-L107","doc":"No singlet below three flavours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weyl_dim_alt_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weyl_dim_alt_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L96-L103","doc":"**The row-cap obstruction.**  The alternating channel `λ = (1³)` is empty\nexactly when `N < 3`.\n\n`ℓ((1³)) = 3`, so Schur–Weyl's row cap `ℓ(λ) ≤ N` admits this partition only\nfor `N ≥ 3`; arithmetically that is `C(N,3) = 0 ↔ N < 3`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:schur-weyl-eightfold","label":"prop:schur-weyl-eightfold","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/schur-weyl-eightfold.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weylDimAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weylDimAlt","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L90-L92","doc":"`dim V_{(1³)}` for `gl_N` — the alternating channel.  The **singlet** when\n`N = 3`.  This is the channel the row cap kills at `N = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weylDimMixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weylDimMixed","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L86-L88","doc":"`dim V_{(2,1)}` for `gl_N` — the mixed channel.  The baryon **octet** when\n`N = 3`.  Equals `N(N²−1)/3`, written division-free as `2·C(N+1,3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weylDimSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction.weylDimSym","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/RowCapObstruction.lean#L82-L84","doc":"`dim V_{(3)}` for `gl_N` — the symmetric channel.  The baryon **decuplet**\nwhen `N = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}